  "turns": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome in. What brings you into the clinic today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S011",
      "patient_response": "Hi. Yeah, um, well, honestly my supervisor is the one who told me I really needed to come see somebody. I work in production, down at the manufacturing plant, and I've been getting in a lot of trouble lately because I just... I keep leaving my station. \n\nIt's like, I'm supposed to stay put right there at my machine on the line, but I just keep wandering off or popping up. Even during our morning shift meetings! We have these pre-shift meetings where everyone is just sitting on these awful metal folding chairs in the breakroom, and I just... I can't stay sitting. I'll just stand up right in the middle of it. And on the floor, it's way worse. My supervisor says it's becoming a really serious safety problem because of all the heavy machinery and the forklifts driving around the aisles. He says I just take off before I even think about it, which, I mean, he's not wrong. I don't even realize I'm doing it until I'm already halfway across the floor. My brain just says 'move' and my legs are already going before I remember I'm supposed to be glued to my spot. \n\nI mean, I get it, safety first and all that, and I'm not trying to cause trouble or get anyone hurt. It's just so hard to just stand in one little square taped off on the concrete for hours. But yeah, that's why I'm here. Because of the walking away thing. He basically said I'm a hazard right now and need to get it figured out.",
